From aba806180dd84b4b546bd01f951c64c8c29e5bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:16:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kernel): read a Solidcraft design's cached final body

camcraft_kernel::solidcraft::import_solidcraft reads a Solidcraft .sc
design (a ZIP container) and returns the final body its model cache
holds, as the same checked solidcore StepSolid the STEP reader hands
out. Only a cache that is provably this document's is read: container
solidcraft-container/1, document solidcraft/<n> in mm, cache format 8
or 10 from solidcraft-truck-adapter/4 on solidcore, and SHA-256 digests
that match document.json and cache/bodies.bin. The final state is
Solidcraft's own rule (last feature not skipped); its one body's slice
is decoded by solidcore-record. Every other case is refused by name:
not a ZIP, ZIP64, multi-disk, encrypted, duplicate names, over 10,000
entries or a size cap, CRC-32 mismatch, no cache, unknown versions, a
stale cache, a payload digest mismatch, bad slices, several bodies, a
placed copy, a mesh body, a bad magic.

The ZIP reader (APPNOTE.TXT) and SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) are written here;
flate2 (already in Cargo.lock) inflates. build_record is split out of
the STEP reader so both share its checks. The maintainer's sample is
the fixture; refusals are pinned on corrupted copies built in the
tests, plus a seeded mutation run under a time bound.

App wiring (open dialog, drop, MCP) is not in this commit.

Refs #1456

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
